{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:14","rows":[{"verses":["87:14"],"words":["مَن تَزَكَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"The successful person is one who purifies himself of idolatry through faith.","anchor":"من تطهّر من الشرك بالإيمان ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:14"],"words":["مَن تَزَكَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن والربيع","stance":"reports","claim":"The successful person has righteous deeds that are pure and growing.","anchor":"من كان صالح عمله زكياً نامياً ،   قاله الحسن والربيع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:14"],"words":["مَن تَزَكَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو الأحوص","stance":"reports","claim":"The phrase refers to paying all the obligatory alms on one's wealth.","anchor":"أنه عنى زكاة الأموال كلها ،   قاله أبو الأحوص","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:14"],"words":["مَن تَزَكَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also allows that it means someone who increases in goodness and righteousness.","anchor":"ويحتمل خامساً : أنه من ازداد خيراً وصلاحاً .","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:15","rows":[{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["وَذَكَرَ ٱسْمَ رَبِّهِۦ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Remembering the Lord means affirming His oneness.","anchor":"أحدها : أن يوحد الله ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["وَذَكَرَ ٱسْمَ رَبِّهِۦ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It can mean invoking God and earnestly asking Him.","anchor":"الثاني : أن يدعوه ويرغب إليه .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["وَذَكَرَ ٱسْمَ رَبِّهِۦ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It can mean asking God's forgiveness and repenting to Him.","anchor":"الثالث : أن يستغفروه ويتوب إليه .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["وَذَكَرَ ٱسْمَ رَبِّهِۦ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"One remembers God inwardly during prayer, fearing punishment and hoping for reward; the prayer's completeness and humility should match that balance.","anchor":"الرابع : أن يذكره بقلبه عند صلاته فيخاف عقابه ويرجو ثوابه ،   ليكون استيفاؤه لها وخشوعه فيها بحسب خوفه ورجائه .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["وَذَكَرَ ٱسْمَ رَبِّهِۦ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It can mean saying God's name aloud when beginning prayer, since prayer is not valid without invoking Him.","anchor":"الخامس : أن يذكر اسم ربه بلسانه عند إحرامه بصلاته ،   لأنها لا تنعقد إلا بذكره .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["وَذَكَرَ ٱسْمَ رَبِّهِۦ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It can mean beginning each sūra with In the name of God, the Merciful, the Compassionate.","anchor":"أن يفتتح كل سورة ببسم الله الرحمن الرحيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["فَصَلَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Prayer refers to the five prescribed daily prayers.","anchor":"أحدها : الصلوات الخمس ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["فَصَلَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو سعيد الخدري","stance":"reports","claim":"Prayer refers to the Eid prayer.","anchor":"الثاني : صلاة العيد{[3249]} ،   قاله أبو سعيد الخدري","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["فَصَلَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو الأحوص","stance":"reports","claim":"Prayer means performing a voluntary prayer after paying alms.","anchor":"الثالث : هو أن يتطوع بصلاة بعد زكاة ،   قاله أبو الأحوص","mentions":[]},{"verses":["87:15"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk reports that the passage was revealed about Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq.","anchor":"وذكر الضحاك أنها نزلت في أبي بكر الصديق رضي الله عنه","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:1","rows":[{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sūrat al-Fajr is Meccan.","anchor":"سورة الفجر مكية بسم الله الرحمان الرحيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God swears by dawn, the breaking of morning light over the eastern horizon.","anchor":"قسم أقسم الله تعالى به ،   وهو انفجار الصبح من أفق المشرق","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The first, false dawn appears as a narrow upright column, then vanishes with darkness between it and morning; it is called the herald of morning, or false because it misleads about morning's arrival.","anchor":"فالأول منهما مستطيل كذنب السرحان يبدو كعمود نور لا عرض له ،   ثم يغيب لظلام يتخلله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The false dawn remains part of the night and does not affect prayer or fasting; legal prayer and fasting times attach to the true dawn.","anchor":"وهو من جملة الليل لا تأثير له في صلاة ولا صوم .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The true dawn spreads across the horizon and is so named because it truthfully announces morning; a cited poet likewise calls it the dawn that confirms morning.","anchor":"وأما الثاني فهو مستطيل النور منتشر في الأفق ويسمى الفجر الصادق لأنه صدقك عن الصبح","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes dawn to mean daytime, named for its beginning.","anchor":"أحدها : أنه عنى به النهار وعبر عنه بالفجر لأنه أوله ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"علي","stance":"reports","claim":"Another takes it as the morning that begins each day's daytime.","anchor":"الثاني : أن الفجر الصبح الذي يبدأ به النهار من كل يوم ،   قاله علّي رضي الله عنه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"A further interpretation takes it as the dawn prayer.","anchor":"الثالث : أنه عنى به صلاة الصبح ،   وهو مروي عن ابن عباس أيضاً","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:1"],"words":["ٱلْفَجْرِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid interprets it as the dawn of the Day of Sacrifice in particular.","anchor":"الرابع : أنه أراد به فجر يوم النحر خاصة ،   قاله مجاهد","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:9","rows":[{"verses":["89:9"],"words":["جَابُوا۟ ٱلصَّخْرَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Thamūd cut, bored, and carved rock into houses; the cited verse about carving mountain homes and a poet's line support this sense.","anchor":"أحدهما : يعني قطعوا الصخر ونقبوه ونحتوه حتى جعلوه بيوتاً ،   كما قال تعالى","mentions":["26:149"]},{"verses":["89:9"],"words":["جَابُوا۟ ٱلصَّخْرَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, they traveled through the valley to take rock, as a cited poet's line about carrying a camel-load through a land illustrates.","anchor":"الثاني : معناه طافوا لأخذ الصخر بالوادي ،   كما قال الشاعر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:9"],"words":["بِٱلْوَادِ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"محمد بن إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Isḥāq identifies the valley as Wādī al-Qurā.","anchor":"فقد زعم محمد بن إسحاق أنه وادي القرى ،   وروى أبو الأشهب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:9"],"words":["بِٱلْوَادِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū al-Ashhab reports from Abū Naḍra that during the Tabūk expedition the Prophet passed through Thamūd's valley and told the party to hurry because it was a cursed valley.","anchor":"وروى أبو الأشهب عن أبي نضرة قال : أتى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:11","rows":[],"none":"verse text only"}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:20","rows":[{"verses":["89:20"],"words":["حُبًّا جَمًّا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Jamman means much or abundant; a cited line by a poet uses the word in the sense of abundant forgiveness.","anchor":"أحدهما : يعني كثيراً ،   قاله ابن عباس ،   والجم الكثير ،   قال الشاعر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:20"],"words":["حُبًّا جَمًّا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan takes it to mean an excessive love that gathers lawful and unlawful wealth together.","anchor":"الثاني : فاحشاً تجمعون حلاله إلى حرامه ،   قاله الحسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:20"],"words":["وَتُحِبُّونَ ٱلْمَالَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests loving wealth so completely that one hoards it and benefits neither religiously nor in worldly life, the worst state for a wealthy person.","anchor":"أنه يحب المال حب إجمام له واستيفاء فلا ينتفع به في دين ولا دنيا","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:24","rows":[{"verses":["89:24"],"words":["قَدَّمْتُ لِحَيَاتِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"The speaker wishes he had sent good deeds from worldly life ahead for his afterlife.","anchor":"أحدهما : قدمت من دنياي لحياتي في الآخرة ،   قاله الضحاك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:24"],"words":["قَدَّمْتُ لِحَيَاتِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is that he wishes he had used his life to prepare for his return in the afterlife.","anchor":"الثاني : قدمت من حياتي لمعادي في الآخرة ذكره ابن عباس","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:27","rows":[{"verses":["89:27"],"words":["ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"The tranquil soul is the believing soul.","anchor":"أحدها : يعني المؤمنة ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:27"],"words":["ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid glosses it as the responsive soul.","anchor":"الثاني : المجيبة ،   قاله مجاهد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:27"],"words":["ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda takes it as the soul that believes what God promised.","anchor":"الثالث : المؤمنة بما وعد الله ،   قاله قتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:27"],"words":["ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أُبيّ بن كعب","stance":"reports","claim":"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb's reading adds secure before tranquil, offering safety as a gloss for the soul.","anchor":"الرابع : الآمنة ،   وهو في حرف أُبيّ بن كعب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:27"],"words":["ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مقاتل","stance":"reports","claim":"Muqātil glosses it as the contented soul.","anchor":"الخامس : الراضية ،   قاله مقاتل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:27"],"words":["ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"بعض أصحاب الخواطر","stance":"reports","claim":"Some contemplative interpreters take it as a soul at rest in worldly life, called to return to its Lord by leaving that attachment.","anchor":"السادس : ما قاله بعض أصحاب الخواطر : المطمئنة إلى الدنيا ،   ارجعي إلى ربك في تركها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:27"],"words":["ٱلنَّفْسُ ٱلْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan says that when God intends to take a believing servant's spirit, the soul is at peace with God and God is at peace with it.","anchor":"السابع : ما قاله الحسن أن الله تعالى إذا أراد أن يقبض روح عبده المؤمن اطمأنت النفس إلى الله عز وجل ،   واطمأن الله إليها","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:28","rows":[{"verses":["89:28"],"words":["ٱرْجِعِيٓ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"The soul is told to return to its body at resurrection.","anchor":"أحدهما : إلى جسدك عند البعث في القيامة ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:28"],"words":["ٱرْجِعِيٓ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو صالح","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, it is told to return to its Lord at death in worldly life.","anchor":"الثاني : إلى ربك عند الموت في الدنيا ،   قاله أبو صالح","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:28"],"words":["ٱرْجِعِيٓ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests a return to the reward of the Lord in the afterlife.","anchor":"ويحتمل تأويلاً ثالثاً : إلى ثواب ربك في الآخرة .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:28"],"words":["رَاضِيَةً مَّرْضِيَّةً"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"The soul is pleased with God, and God is pleased with it.","anchor":"أحدهما : رضيت عن الله ورضي عنها ،   قاله الحسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:28"],"words":["رَاضِيَةً مَّرْضِيَّةً"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"The soul is pleased with God's reward, and God is pleased with its deeds.","anchor":"الثاني : رضيت بثواب الله ورضي بعملها ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:29","rows":[{"verses":["89:29"],"words":["فِي عِبَادِي"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أُبيّ بن كعب","stance":"reports","claim":"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb's reading has the singular, enter among My servant.","anchor":"أحدها : في عبدي ،   وهو في حرف أُبيّ بن كعب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:29"],"words":["فِي عِبَادِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"The phrase can mean enter into My obedience.","anchor":"الثاني : في طاعتي ،   قاله الضحاك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:29"],"words":["فِي عِبَادِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"It can mean enter among My servants.","anchor":"الثالث : معناه فادخلي{[3264]} مع عبادي ،   قاله السدي","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:89:30","rows":[{"verses":["89:30"],"words":["جَنَّتِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"The garden can mean God's mercy.","anchor":"أحدهما : في رحمتي ،   قاله الضحاك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:30"],"words":["جَنَّتِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الجمهور","stance":"reports","claim":"Most interpreters take it as the eternal home and dwelling of the righteous.","anchor":"الثاني : الجنة التي هي دار الخلود ومسكن الأبرار ،   وهو قول الجمهور","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:30"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أسامة بن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Usāma ibn Zayd says the tranquil soul is given glad tidings of Paradise at death, at resurrection, and in Paradise itself.","anchor":"وقال أسامة بن زيد : بشرت النفس المطمئنة بالجنة عند الموت ،   وعند البعث وفي الجنة .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:30"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās reports that the verse was revealed while Abū Bakr sat with the Prophet; Abū Bakr admired it, and the Prophet said it would be said to him.","anchor":"فروى ابن عباس أنها نزلت وأبو بكر جالس فقال : يا رسول الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:30"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk says it was revealed about ʿUthmān when he endowed the Rūma well in Medina.","anchor":"الثاني : أنها نزلت في عثمان حين وقف بئر رومة{[3265]} ،   قاله الضحاك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:30"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"بريدة الأسلمي","stance":"reports","claim":"Burayda al-Aslamī says it was revealed about Ḥamza.","anchor":"الثالث : أنها نزلت في حمزة ،   قاله بريدة الأسلمي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["89:30"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عكرمة والفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿIkrima and al-Farrāʾ transmit the view that the verse applies generally to all believers.","anchor":"الرابع : أنها عامة في كل المؤمنين ،   رواه عكرمة والفراء","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:90:6","rows":[{"verses":["90:6"],"words":["مَالًا لُّبَدًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lubadan can mean plentiful; a cited line uses jamm in the sense of abundant forgiveness.","anchor":"{ يقول أهلكت مالاً لبداً } فيه وجهان : أحدهما : يعني كثيراً","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:6"],"words":["مَالًا لُّبَدًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It can mean wealth heaped together, as felt is called libd because its fibers gather and mat together.","anchor":"الثاني : مجتمعاً بعضه على بعض ،   ومنه سمي اللبد لاجتماعه وتلبيد بعضه على بعض","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:6"],"words":["مَالًا لُّبَدًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It may mean old wealth, either deriving from eternity or emphasizing age by comparison to Labid, whom Arabs used as an exemplar of great age.","anchor":"ويحتمل ثالثاً : يعني مالاً قديماً ،   لاشتقاقه من الأبد ،   أو للمبالغة في قدمه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:6"],"words":["أَهْلَكْتُ مَالًا"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"One reported identification is Abū al-Shadd al-Jumaḥī, who spent abundant wealth opposing the Messenger and blocking God's way.","anchor":"وقيل إن هذا القائل أبو الشد الجمحي ،   أنفق مالا كثيراً في عداوة رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم والصد عن سبيل الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:6"],"words":["أَهْلَكْتُ مَالًا"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another reported identification is al-Naḍr ibn al-Ḥārith.","anchor":"وقيل بل هو{[3271]} النضر بن الحارث .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:6"],"words":["أَهْلَكْتُ مَالًا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If the speaker is boasting about what he spent, that is an act of transgression.","anchor":"أن يكون استطالة بما أنفق فيكون طغياناً منه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:6"],"words":["أَهْلَكْتُ مَالًا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, he regrets the spending and laments its loss.","anchor":"الثاني : أن يكون أسفاً عليه ،   فيكون ندماً منه .","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:90:7","rows":[{"verses":["90:7"],"words":["أَن لَّمْ يَرَهُۥٓ أَحَدٌ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid takes the unseen witness to be God: does the person think God did not see him?","anchor":"أحدهما : أن لم يره الله ،   قاله مجاهد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:7"],"words":["أَن لَّمْ يَرَهُۥٓ أَحَدٌ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن شجرة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Shajara takes it to mean that no person saw what he spent.","anchor":"الثاني : أن لم يره أحد من الناس فيما أنفقه ،   قاله ابن شجرة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["90:7"],"words":["أَن لَّمْ يَرَهُۥٓ أَحَدٌ"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also reads it as a threat: the person thinks his deed will not be exposed or punished; the two earlier readings instead charge him with denial.","anchor":"ويحتمل وجهاً ثالثاً : أيحسب أن لم يظهر ما فعله أن لا يؤاخذ به ،   على وجه التهديد","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:91:11","rows":[{"verses":["91:11"],"words":["بِطَغْوَىٰهَآ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد وقتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid and Qatāda take the phrase to mean Thamūd's transgression and disobedience.","anchor":"أحدها : بطغيانها ومعصيتها ،   قاله مجاهد وقتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["91:11"],"words":["بِطَغْوَىٰهَآ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"محمد بن كعب","stance":"reports","claim":"Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb glosses it as meaning all of Thamūd collectively.","anchor":"الثاني : بأجمعها ،   قاله محمد بن كعب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["91:11"],"words":["بِطَغْوَىٰهَآ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās takes it as the punishment that came upon them; they said the punishment itself was named Ṭagwā.","anchor":"الثالث : بعذابها ،   قاله ابن عباس . قالوا كان اسم العذاب الذي جاءها الطغوى","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:4","rows":[{"verses":["92:4"],"words":["سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The people's endeavors differ in their outcomes: some are rewarded with Paradise and others punished in the Fire.","anchor":"لمختلف الجزاء فمنكم مثاب بالجنة ومنكم معاقب بالنار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:4"],"words":["سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Their actions also differ: some are believers and others unbelievers, righteous and wicked, obedient and disobedient.","anchor":"لمختلف الأفعال منكم مؤمن وكافر وبر وفاجر ومطيع وعاص","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:4"],"words":["سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that temperaments differ, from compassionate to harsh, mild to reckless, and generous to miserly.","anchor":"لمختلف الأخلاق فمنكم راحم وقاس وحليم وطائش وجواد وبخيل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:4"],"words":["إِنَّ سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتَّىٰ"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"On the interpretation about differing temperaments, the oath is directed to this point.","anchor":"وعلى هذا وقع القسم وروى ابن مسعود أن هذه الآية نزلت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:4"],"words":["إِنَّ سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتَّىٰ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن مسعود","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Masʿūd reports that it was revealed about Abū Bakr and Umayya and Ubayy, the sons of Khalaf, torturing Bilāl for becoming Muslim; Abū Bakr bought Bilāl for a cloak and ten coins and freed him for God.","anchor":"روى ابن مسعود أن هذه الآية نزلت في أبي بكر وفي أمية وأبي ابني خلف حين عذبا بلالاً على إسلامه","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:5","rows":[{"verses":["92:5"],"words":["مَنْ أَعْطَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن مسعود","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Masʿūd identifies the giver in the verse as Abū Bakr.","anchor":"قال ابن مسعود يعني أبا بكر .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:5"],"words":["أَعْطَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Giving means spending one's wealth.","anchor":"أحدها : من بذل ماله ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:5"],"words":["وَٱتَّقَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Being God-fearing means avoiding the prohibitions God has forbidden.","anchor":"الثاني : اتقى محارم الله التي نهى عنها , قاله قتادة .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:5"],"words":["وَٱتَّقَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, it means avoiding miserliness.","anchor":"الثالث : اتقى البخل ،   قاله مجاهد","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:6","rows":[{"verses":["92:6"],"words":["بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk glosses al-ḥusnā as God's oneness, expressed in the testimony There is no god but God.","anchor":"أحدها : بتوحيد الله ،   وهو قول لا إله إلا الله ،   قاله الضحاك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:6"],"words":["بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda takes it as what God has promised.","anchor":"الثاني : بموعود الله ،   قاله قتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:6"],"words":["بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid glosses it as Paradise.","anchor":"الثالث : بالجنة ،   قاله مجاهد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:6"],"words":["بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"خصيف","stance":"reports","claim":"Khuṣayf takes it as reward.","anchor":"الرابع : بالثواب ،   قاله خصيف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:6"],"words":["بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"زيد بن أسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"Zayd ibn Aslam takes it as prayer, alms, and fasting.","anchor":"الخامس : بالصلاة والزكاة والصوم ،   قاله زيد بن أسلم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:6"],"words":["بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"عطاء","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAṭāʾ interprets it as believing what God has bestowed upon him.","anchor":"السادس : بما أنعم الله عليه ،   قاله عطاء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:6"],"words":["بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan takes it as trusting that God will replace what one gives; Māwardī notes that most of these glosses are close in meaning.","anchor":"السابع : بالخلف من عطائه ،   قاله الحسن ،   ومعاني أكثرها متقاربة","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:7","rows":[{"verses":["92:7"],"words":["لِلْيُسْرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-yusrā means goodness.","anchor":"أحدهما : للخير ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:7"],"words":["لِلْيُسْرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"زيد بن أسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-yusrā means Paradise.","anchor":"الثاني : للجنة ،   قاله زيد بن أسلم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:7"],"words":["لِلْيُسْرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that God will make the means to goodness and righteousness easy until doing them is easy for the person.","anchor":"فسنيسر له أسباب الخير والصلاح حتى يسهل عليه فعلها","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:8","rows":[{"verses":["92:8"],"words":["مَنۢ بَخِلَ وَٱسْتَغْنَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن مسعود","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Masʿūd identifies the miserly, self-sufficient people as Umayya and Ubayy, the sons of Khalaf.","anchor":"قال ابن مسعود : يعني بذلك\nأمية وأبياً ابني خلف .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:8"],"words":["بَخِلَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس والحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Being miserly means withholding one's wealth, which will not last.","anchor":"أحدهما : بخل بماله الذي لا يبقى ،   قاله ابن عباس والحسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:8"],"words":["بَخِلَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, it means withholding God's due.","anchor":"الثاني : بخل بحق الله تعالى ،   قاله قتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:8"],"words":["وَٱسْتَغْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan takes self-sufficiency as relying on one's wealth.","anchor":"أحدهما : بماله ،   قاله الحسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:8"],"words":["وَٱسْتَغْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās takes it as feeling independent of one's Lord.","anchor":"الثاني : عن ربه ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:9","rows":[{"verses":["92:9"],"words":["وَكَذَّبَ بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī says the seven interpretations of al-ḥusnā given for the preceding verse also apply here.","anchor":"{ وكذب بالحسنى } فيه التأويلات السبعة{[3282]} .","mentions":["92:6"]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:10","rows":[{"verses":["92:10"],"words":["لِلْعُسْرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-ʿusrā means evil from God.","anchor":"أحدهما : للشر من الله تعالى ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:10"],"words":["لِلْعُسْرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن مسعود","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-ʿusrā means the Fire.","anchor":"الثاني : للنار ،   قاله ابن مسعود","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:10"],"words":["لِلْعُسْرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that God makes the means to goodness and righteousness difficult until doing them is hard for the person.","anchor":"فسنعسر عليه أسباب الخير والصلاح حتى يصعب عليه فعلها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:10"],"words":["فَسَنُيَسِّرُهُۥ لِلْعُسْرَىٰ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū al-Dardāʾ reports from the Prophet, through Qatāda and Khulayd, that each sunrise two angels ask God to replace the giver and bring loss to the one who withholds; the Prophet then recites the giving passage and the following verse.","anchor":"يروي قتادة عن خليد عن أبي الدرداء أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال : \" ما من يوم طلعت فيه شمسه إلا","mentions":["92:5","92:6"]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:11","rows":[{"verses":["92:11"],"words":["إِذَا تَرَدَّىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو صالح وزيد بن أسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"The person is unable to use his wealth when he falls into the Fire.","anchor":"أحدهما : إذا تردى في النار ،   قاله أبو صالح وزيد بن أسلم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:11"],"words":["إِذَا تَرَدَّىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد وقتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, he has died and fallen into his grave.","anchor":"الثاني : إذا مات فتردى في قبره ،   قاله مجاهد وقتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:11"],"words":["إِذَا تَرَدَّىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that he has sunk into error and fallen into acts of disobedience.","anchor":"إذا تردى في ضلاله وهوى في معاصيه","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:12","rows":[{"verses":["92:12"],"words":["لَلْهُدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"يحيى بن سلام","stance":"reports","claim":"God's guidance means making clear the paths of guidance and misguidance.","anchor":"أن نبين سبل الهدى والضلالة قاله يحيى بن سلام","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:12"],"words":["لَلْهُدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda interprets it as explaining what is lawful and unlawful.","anchor":"الثاني : بيان الحلال والحرام ،   قاله قتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:12"],"words":["لَلْهُدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that God undertakes the reward for the guidance He has given.","anchor":"علينا ثواب هداه الذي هدينا","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:13","rows":[{"verses":["92:13"],"words":["لَلْءَاخِرَةَ وَٱلْأُولَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الكلبي والفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kalbī and al-Farrāʾ take the two lives to mean their rewards in this world and the next.","anchor":"أحدهما : ثواب الدنيا والآخرة ،   قاله الكلبي والفراء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:13"],"words":["لَلْءَاخِرَةَ وَٱلْأُولَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مقاتل","stance":"reports","claim":"Muqātil takes them to mean God's dominion over this world and the next.","anchor":"الثاني : ملك الدنيا وملك الآخرة ،   قاله مقاتل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:13"],"words":["لَلْءَاخِرَةَ وَٱلْأُولَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that God is the one who recompenses people in both worlds.","anchor":"الله المجازي في الدنيا والآخرة","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:15","rows":[{"verses":["92:15"],"words":["ٱلْأَشْقَى"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-ashqā means the wretched one.","anchor":"{ لا يَصلاها إلا الأشْقَى } أي الشقّي .","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:92:16","rows":[{"verses":["92:16"],"words":["كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda says he denied God's Book and turned away from obedience to God.","anchor":"أحدهما : كذب بكتاب الله وتولى عن طاعة الله ،   قاله قتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["92:16"],"words":["كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Another interpretation is that he denied the Messenger and turned away from obeying him.","anchor":"كذب الرسول وتولى عن طاعته","mentions":[]}]}
