{"loc":"MAWARDI:93:1","rows":[{"verses":["93:1"],"words":["ٱلضُّحَىٰ"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"الجميع","stance":"reports","claim":"Sūrat al-Ḍuḥā is Meccan according to all authorities.","anchor":"سورة الضحى مكية في قول الجميع بسم الله الرحمان الرحيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:1"],"words":["ٱلضُّحَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḍuḥā may mean the first hour of day, when the sun has moved on.","anchor":"أحدها : أنه أول ساعة من النهار إذا ترحلت الشمس ،   قاله السدي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:1"],"words":["ٱلضُّحَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda takes it as the beginning of the day.","anchor":"الثاني : أنه صدر النهار ،   قاله قتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:1"],"words":["ٱلضُّحَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قطرب","stance":"reports","claim":"Quṭrub interprets it as sunrise.","anchor":"الثالث : هو طلوع الشمس ،   قاله قطرب .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:1"],"words":["ٱلضُّحَىٰ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid takes it as daylight throughout the day; the derivation, attributed to ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā, comes from appearing in the sun.","anchor":"الرابع : هو ضوء النهار في اليوم كله ،   مأخوذ من قولهم ضحى فلان الشمس ،   إذا ظهر لها ،   قاله مجاهد ،   والاشتقاق لعلي بن عيسى","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:93:6","rows":[{"verses":["93:6"],"words":["يَتِيمًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"An orphan is one whose father has died; the Prophet lost his parents while young, was raised by his grandfather ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and then by his uncle Abū Ṭālib.","anchor":"واليتيم بموت الأب ،   وقد كان رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقد أبويه وهو صغير ،   فكفله جده عبد المطلب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:6"],"words":["فَـَٔاوَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مقاتل","stance":"reports","claim":"On the literal orphan reading, God gave the Prophet a home and a compassionate guardian to raise and support him after ʿAbd Allāh and ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib died.","anchor":"أحدهما : أي جعل لك مأوى لتربيتك ،   وقيمّاً يحنو عليك ويكفلك وهو أبو طالب بعد موت عبد الله وعبد المطلب ،   قاله مقاتل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:6"],"words":["فَـَٔاوَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الكلبي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kalbī instead says God gave the Prophet a home of his own and freed him from needing Abū Ṭālib's guardianship.","anchor":"الثاني : أي جعل لك مأوى نفسك ،   وأغناك عن كفالة أبي طالب ،   قاله الكلبي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:6"],"words":["يَتِيمًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, yatīm can mean unique and without equal, as in the expression for a pearl with no match.","anchor":"والوجه الثاني : أنه أراد باليتيم الذي لا مثيل له ولا نظير ،   من قولهم درة يتيمة ،   إذا لم يكن لها مثيل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:6"],"words":["فَـَٔاوَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"With the unique-person sense, God may have drawn the Prophet near and chosen him for His message.","anchor":"فآواك إلى نفسه واختصك برسالته","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:6"],"words":["فَـَٔاوَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, God made him a refuge for orphans and caretaker of people after he had been an orphan and cared for himself, recalling God's blessings.","anchor":"الثاني : أن جعلك مأوى الأيتام بعد أن كنت يتيماً ،   وكفيل الأنام بعد أن كنت مكفولاً ،   تذكيراً بنعمه عليه ،   وهو محتمل","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:93:7","rows":[{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عيسى","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿĪsā says God found the Prophet not knowing the truth and guided him to it.","anchor":"أحدها : وجدك لا تعرف الحق فهداك إليه ،   قاله ابن عيسى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الطبري","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ṭabarī takes it as God finding him without prophethood and guiding him to it.","anchor":"الثاني : ووجدك ضالاً عن النبوة فهداك إليها ،   قاله الطبري","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddī's sense is that God found the Prophet's people astray and guided him to show them the way.","anchor":"الثالث : ووجد قومك في ضلال فهداك إلى إرشادهم ،   وهذا معنى قول السدي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Another possibility is that God found him away from the migration and guided him to it.","anchor":"ووجدك ضالاً عن الهجرة فهداك إليها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It may mean forgetful, with God reminding him, as in the wording about one of the two women forgetting.","anchor":"الخامس : ووجدك ناسياً فأذكرك ،   كما قال تعالى : { أن تضل إحداهما }","mentions":["2:282"]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It may mean seeking: he was seeking the direction of prayer, and the lost person is called seeking because he searches for the way.","anchor":"السادس : ووجدك طالباً القبلة فهداك إليها ،   ويكون الضلال بمعنى الطلب ،   لأن الضال طالب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It may mean perplexed: he was uncertain how to explain what had been revealed, and a lost person is perplexed.","anchor":"السابع : ووجدك متحيراً في بيان ما نزل عليك فهداك إليه ،   فيكون الضلال بمعنى التحير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It may mean lost or neglected among his people, with God guiding him to Himself; a lost person is also one who is forsaken.","anchor":"الثامن : ووجدك ضائعاً في قومك فهداك إليه ،   ويكون الضلال بمعنى الضياع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["ضَآلًّا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It may mean loving guidance: God found him loving it and led him to it; the cited verse uses dalāl for Jacob's love, and two poetic lines offer further evidence.","anchor":"التاسع : ووجدك محباً للهداية فهداك إليها ،   ويكون الضلال بمعنى المحبة","mentions":["12:95"]},{"verses":["93:7"],"words":["وَوَجَدَكَ ضَآلًّا فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan reads it with the lost one as subject and passive guidance: God found the astray one, who was then guided through you.","anchor":"وقرأ الحسن : ووجدَك ضالٌّ فهُدِي ،   أي وجَدَك الضالُّ فاهتدى بك","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:93:8","rows":[{"verses":["93:8"],"words":["عَآئِلًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash takes ʿāʾilan as someone with dependents; God provided for the Prophet, as a cited poetic line about the needy traveler illustrates.","anchor":"أحدها : وجدك ذا عيال{[3289]} فكفاك ،   قاله الأخفش ،   ومنه قول جرير :","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:8"],"words":["عَآئِلًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ glosses it as poor, whom God made comfortable; a cited poem uses yaʿīlu to mean becoming poor.","anchor":"الثاني : فقيراً فيسر لك ،   قاله الفراء ،   قال الشاعر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:8"],"words":["فَأَغْنَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that the Prophet was poor in proofs and arguments, and God enriched him with them.","anchor":"الثالث : أي وجدك فقيراً من الحجج والبراهين ،   فأغناك بها .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["93:8"],"words":["عَآئِلًا فَأَغْنَىٰ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"A report says the Prophet loudly repeated three times that his Lord bestows upon him, and is worthy of bestowing; this offers a reading in which God enriched the poor person through him.","anchor":"الرابع : ووجدك العائل الفقير فأغناه الله بك ،   روي أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال بصوته الأعلى ثلاث مرات","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:95:4","rows":[{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"One view takes humankind collectively, using the singular for emphasis because the quality described applies to everyone.","anchor":"أحدهما : أنه أراد عموم الناس ،   وذكر الإنسان على وجه التكثير لأنه وصفه بما يعم لجميع الناس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, it may refer to one particular person who is described by a quality shared by people generally.","anchor":"الثاني : أنه أراد إنساناً بعينه عناه بهذه الصفة ،   وإن كان صفة الناس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās identifies the particular person as Kulda ibn Asīd.","anchor":"أحدها : أنه عنى كلدة بن أسيد ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"مقاتل","stance":"reports","claim":"Muqātil identifies him as Abū Jahl.","anchor":"الثاني : أبا جهل ،   قاله مقاتل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A further identification in the surviving text is the Messenger of God.","anchor":"الخامس : أنه عنى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["فِيٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"The phrase means the most balanced form of creation.","anchor":"أحدها : في أعدل خلق ،   قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["فِيٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو العالية","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū al-ʿĀliya interprets it as the finest image.","anchor":"الثاني : في أحسن صورة ،   قاله أبو العالية","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["فِيٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿIkrima takes it to mean youth and strength.","anchor":"الثالث : في شباب وقوة ،   قاله عكرمة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["فِيٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Another report from Ibn ʿAbbās says it means upright stature, unlike other animals, which are bent over.","anchor":"الرابع : منتصب القامة ،   لأن سائر الحيوان منكب غير الإنسان ،   فإنه منتصب ،   وهو مروي عن ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["فِيٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests the most complete intellect, since a person's proper formation rests on reason.","anchor":"ويحتمل خامساً : أي في أكمل عقل ،   لأن تقويم الإنسان بعقله ،   وعلى هذا وقع القسم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["95:4"],"words":["فِيٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"On the interpretation that human perfection lies in intellect, the oath is directed to that point.","anchor":"لأن تقويم الإنسان بعقله ،   وعلى هذا وقع القسم","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:96:1","rows":[{"verses":["96:1"],"words":["ٱقْرَأْ بِٱسْمِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sūrat al-ʿAlaq is Meccan by consensus.","anchor":"سورة العلق مكية إجماعا بسم الله الرحمان الرحيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:1"],"words":["ٱقْرَأْ بِٱسْمِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عبيد بن عمير","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr reports that Gabriel first came to the Prophet with a namat, pressed him to read three times, and after the third, forceful pressing, the Prophet answered that he was not a reader before Gabriel recited this verse.","anchor":"روي عن عبيد بن عمير قال : جاء جبريل إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أول ما أتاه بنمط","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:1"],"words":["ٱقْرَأْ بِٱسْمِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The instruction means to begin reciting in the name of the Lord who created.","anchor":"أي استفتح قراءتك باسم ربك الذي خلق","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:1"],"words":["ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The wording distinguishes God as Creator because Quraysh worshipped other gods, none of which created; naming the Creator removes ambiguity.","anchor":"لأن قريشاً كانت تعبد آلهة ليس فيهم خالق غيره تعالى ،   فميز نفسه بذلك ليزول عنه الالتباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:1"],"words":["ٱقْرَأْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عائشة","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿĀʾisha reports the order of revelation: this was first, followed by Sūrat Nūn wa-l-Qalam, al-Muddaththir, and al-Ḍuḥā.","anchor":"روت عائشة رضي الله عنها أنها أول سورة نزلت على رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ثم بعدها","mentions":["68:1","74:1","93:1"]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:96:2","rows":[{"verses":["96:2"],"words":["ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Here humankind means all people, created from a clot after the sperm-drop.","anchor":"يريد بالإنسان جنس الناس كلهم ،   خلقوا من علق بعد النطفة ،","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:2"],"words":["عَلَقٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alaq is the plural of ʿalaqa, a piece of wet blood named for sticking to what it touches; once dry, it is no longer a clot. A cited poem describes it clinging to the vein.","anchor":"والعلقة قطعة من دم رطب سميت بذلك لأنها تعلق لرطوبتها بما تمر عليه ،   فإذا جفت لم تكن علقة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This can show God's bounty: from a lowly clot He made a sound, rational, discerning human being.","anchor":"أن يبين قدر نعمته على الإنسان بأن خلقه من علقة مهينة حتى صار بشراً سوياً وعاقلاً متميزاً","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"It can also parallel God's moving the human from stage to stage with His moving the Prophet from ignorance to prophethood until he was fully prepared.","anchor":"كذلك نقلك من الجهالة إلى النبوة حتى تستكمل محلها","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:96:3","rows":[{"verses":["96:3"],"words":["وَرَبُّكَ ٱلْأَكْرَمُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-akram means the Generous.","anchor":"{ اقرأ وربك الأكرم } أي الكريم .","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:3"],"words":["ٱقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ ٱلْأَكْرَمُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, read it as recite knowing that your Lord is the Most Generous: the blessings just mentioned point to His generosity.","anchor":"ويحتمل ثانياً : اقرأ بأن ربك هو الأكرم ،   لأنه لما ذكر ما تقدم من نعمه دل بها على نعمة كرمه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:3"],"words":["ٱلْأَكْرَمُ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"إبراهيم بن عيسى اليشكري","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibrāhīm ibn ʿĪsā al-Yashkurī illustrates God's generosity by saying He provides for His servant while the servant worships another.","anchor":"قال إبراهيم بن عيسى اليشكري : من كرمه أن يرزق عبده وهو يعبد غيره","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:96:4","rows":[{"verses":["96:4"],"words":["بِٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God taught the writer to write with the pen.","anchor":"أي علم الكاتب أن يكتب بالقلم ،   وسمي قلماً لأنه يقلم ،","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:4"],"words":["بِٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qalam is named from the verb meaning to cut, as in trimming a fingernail.","anchor":"وسمي قلماً لأنه يقلم ،   أي : يقطع ،   ومنه تقليم الظفر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:4"],"words":["عَلَّمَ بِٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid reports from Ibn ʿUmar that God created four things with His hand and told the rest of creation to be: the pen, Throne, Garden of Eden, and Adam.","anchor":"وروى مجاهد عن ابن عمر قال : خلق الله تعالى أربعة أشياء بيده ،   ثم قال لسائر الخلق : كن ،   فكان القلم والعرش وجنة عدن وآدم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:4"],"words":["عَلَّمَ بِٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"كعب الأحبار","stance":"reports","claim":"Kaʿb al-Aḥbār says the person taught by the pen was Adam, the first to write.","anchor":"أحدها : أنه أراد آدم عليه السلام ،   لأنه أول من كتب ،   قاله كعب الأحبار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:4"],"words":["عَلَّمَ بِٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk identifies him as Idrīs, the first to write.","anchor":"الثاني : إدريس ،   وهو أول من كتب ،   قاله الضحاك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:4"],"words":["عَلَّمَ بِٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also says this means everyone who writes, since all writing is learned through God's teaching; this joins the blessings of creation and instruction.","anchor":"الثالث : أنه أراد كل من كتب بالقلم ؛ لأنه ما علم إلا بتعليم الله له","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:96:5","rows":[{"verses":["96:5"],"words":["مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة وابن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda and Ibn Zayd take what God taught as writing with the pen.","anchor":"أحدهما : الخط بالقلم ،   قاله قتادة وابن زيد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:5"],"words":["مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن شجرة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Shajara interprets it as teaching every craft a person learns.","anchor":"الثاني : علمه كل صنعة علمها فتعلم ،   قاله ابن شجرة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["96:5"],"words":["مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Māwardī also suggests that God taught the human, through the initial state of creation, evidence of how He created him and could later move him according to His will.","anchor":"ويحتمل ثالثاً : علمه من حاله في ابتداء خلقه ما يستدل به على خلقه ،   وأن ينقله من بعد على إرادته","mentions":[]}]}
